    "summary": "Final build and sweeps: tsc --noEmit clean; planner (180 tests, 177 pass, 3 skipped, 0 fail), orchestrator (77/74/3 skipped), classifier, executor, explore, runtimes, summariser, daemon analyze-rpc and the context tests that import the planner all show 0 failures. The wider src/analyze/context sweep did not finish inside 570 s twice and is not tied to this change. Live docs-broad regression run on the daemon at 6e79e62e4 (run docs-broad-live-mwcdxpq5), recorded as a REPORTED FAIL: the plan stage passed (20 tasks, inside the XL focused 20-80 band on all three attempts; attempt 1 INV-7, attempt 2 INV-10, attempt 3 accepted) but the execute stage had produced 6 of 20 task outputs when the test's 40-minute limit ended it, so no final report was reached. Cause seen in the run tree: the XL root plan spawns five L-sized child plans (about 100+ serial model-driven tasks, a 13.7 MB inventory); this is an execute-cost / size-to-depth issue outside this Story and will be triaged separately.",
